This directory carries one file into the game image: pack.sh, the server-files
profile that the FreeBSD installer uses.

It is here for a single function, pack_apply_rates(), which knows which columns
of mob_proto.txt carry experience and yang, which lines of the three drop
tables carry a chance, and how to rewrite them from an untouched baseline. The
panel's "Server rates" page ends up in that function on FreeBSD and, through
m2-rates in this image, on Linux too -- one implementation, not two that can
drift apart.

It is staged here by ../../prepare-context.sh from

    files/packs/tmp4-r40250.pack

and is deliberately not committed: the copy in files/packs is the real one.

Without it the image still builds and runs; the rates page then reports that
these server files cannot have their rates changed, which is the truth.
